sections.text:
The go-to formation for Haunted Mines is 1-4:
1 Hero, the Offlaner, covers the top lane;
4 Heroes cover the bottom lane.

As shown in the image below, Haunted Mines has a total of 4 Mercenary Camps:
1 Sapper Camp (purple icon) near the center of the top lane;
1 Siege Camp (green icon) on the left side of the top lane;
1 Siege Camp (green icon) on the right side of the bottom lane;
1 Sapper Camp (purple icon) near the center of the bottom lane.
Mercenary Camps on Haunted Mines are always active,
even when the Mines are open or Grave Golems are in lane.

At the beginning of the Objective phase, 8 groups of Risen Miners
and 1 Grave Golem will spawn in the Mines. They drop Cursed Skulls.
The 8 groups of Risen Miners are spread around the Mines but they always spawn in the
same locations. The underground Grave Golem always spawns in the center of the Mines.

To give you an overview, the Undead Army is arranged as follows:
2 groups of 5 Risen Miners on the top-right;
2 groups of 4 Risen Miners on the bottom-right;
2 groups of 5 Risen Miners on the bottom-left;
2 groups of 4 Risen Miners on the top-left;
1 underground Grave Golem in the center.
In addition to dropping Cursed Skulls, the underground Grave Golem
also drops Regeneration Globes when reaching 70% Health and 30% Health.
